# tests/rgrep, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. Every assertion is about a run's RESULT, and dispatching a run
# is what a worker does with `curry` + `run-then`. `rgrep` resolves to the built
# worker by being named; `tree` is the fixture it greps.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --rgrep:@=DEEP-DEPS/rgrep --tree:@=tree
